  "question": {
    "text": "Two capacitors <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> in a circuit are joined as shown in the figure. The potentials of points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> respectively. Then the potential of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> will be<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0027_d410f4938024.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 35px;\" />"
